  <data name="Window.Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>BetterRTX Manager</value></data>
  <data name="ManualSelectionIntroText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>The app couldn't auto-locate your game files using the usual fast methods!&#x0a;A system-wide scan is in progress, there is a high chance it will find your game given enough time.</value></data>
  <data name="ManualSelectionText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>But if it is taking too long? Click to manually navigate to the folder where the game is installed to, it should have a file called Minecraft.Windows.exe inside of it.&#x0a;&#x0a;The app is tolerant towards slightly imprecise location selections, it will still try to have a look around no matter where you select, but if you're still having trouble finding out where your game is installed to, join the Vanilla RTX Discord server and ask for help, or try to find out online.</value></data>
  <data name="EmptyStateText.Text" xml:space="preserve"><value>No BetterRTX presets cached</value></data>

  <data name="RefreshButton_ToolTip" xml:space="preserve"><value>Resets cache, clearing all imported presets and downloaded files from BetterRTX API, forcing a refetch.&#x0a;&#x0a;Note: This happens automatically whenever Minecraft is updated (always) or periodically whenever changes in the API are detected (possibly, but not guranteed), hence this button exists for you to trigger a manual refresh in case BetterRTX delievers its updates with a delay or the API pretends to remain the same after rolling out updates.&#x0a;&#x0a;Note 2: This button won't clear your Default RTX preset, which is backed up upon your first attempt at installing a preset. Only game updates can trigger a reset of Default preset, so ultimately the app can pick up the new defaults fresh from the new update of your game.</value></data>

  <data name="WindowTitle_Release" xml:space="preserve"><value>BetterRTX Preset Manager - Minecraft Release</value></data>

  <data name="Disclaimer_Title" xml:space="preserve"><value>Third-Party API Usage Notice</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_Body" xml:space="preserve"><value>BetterRTX is an unofficial mod to Minecraft RTX's shader code. The files for this feature are provided by the following third-party: https://bedrock.graphics/api
BetterRTX can also potentially break with Minecraft updates. Vanilla RTX App takes extensive measures to mitigate any issues that may arise, such as giving a way to quickly revert to your defaults.

Please pay attention to the info panels to keep updated and help steer yourself away from potential issues.</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_ConfirmButton" xml:space="preserve"><value>I understand the risks and wish to continue</value></data>
  <data name="Disclaimer_DismissButton" xml:space="preserve"><value>Dismiss</value></data>

  <data name="Status_PreviewNotSupported" xml:space="preserve"><value>BetterRTX Preset Manager does not support Minecraft Preview, the API only provides files intended for stable Minecraft releases that may not work on the latest Preview.</value></data>
